<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ælfthryth, Countess of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 877–<a href="/years/929">929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Elftrude</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ælfthryth was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, and the wife of Baldwin II, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, whom she married in the 890s. The marriage linked the young Flemish principality to the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> royal house, and through her son Arnulf I she was an ancestor of the later counts of Flanders and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-flanders">Matilda of Flanders</a>, wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aelfthryth-countess-of-flanders.jpg" alt="Ælfthryth, Countess of Flanders" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baldwin_II_and_%C3%86lfthryth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
